<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhumibol Adulyadej</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1927">1927</a>–<a href="/years/2016">2016</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Rama IX</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhumibol Adulyadej, also known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama">Rama</a> IX, was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a> from 1946 until his death in 2016, the longest reign in Thai history. Coming to the throne after the death of his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ananda-mahidol">Ananda Mahidol</a>, he became a revered figure and an arbiter in political crises, while the monarchy's prestige grew under military governments. He was succeeded by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vajiralongkorn">Vajiralongkorn</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bhumibol-adulyadej.jpg" alt="Bhumibol Adulyadej" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harry Pot / Anefo · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aankomst_Koning_Bhumibol_en_Koningin_Sirikit_te_Den_Haag,_Koning_Bhumibol,_Bestanddeelnr_911-6993_(cropped)(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
